No licence has been granted yet.

This file records the current, accurate legal state rather than pretending to a
licence that has not been chosen: the source is published so that competition
judges and the teaching department can read, run and verify it, and no rights to
copy, modify, redistribute or use it beyond that are granted at this time.

If you want the project reusable, replace this file with a real licence before
publication. Three options that actually fit this project:

  MIT
    Shortest path to "anyone may use and adapt this". Appropriate if the aim is
    for other teaching departments to be able to run and modify ClerkMate.

  Apache-2.0
    Same permissiveness as MIT plus an explicit patent grant and a requirement
    that changes be stated. Appropriate if the project may later involve
    institutional or commercial contributors.

  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for the educational content, MIT for the code
    A split licence. The clinical content — the 66 completeness requirements,
    the 57 risk factors, the level rules, the demo cases — is teaching material
    rather than software, and a content licence fits it better than a code one.

Note on the rating scales: PHQ, GAD and Mini-Cog are free to use, and their
items ship with the app. HADS (Snaith & Zigmond) and ISI (Morin) are licensed
instruments; ClerkMate deliberately does not reproduce their items and records
only a score entered from an official form. Whichever licence is chosen for
ClerkMate does not and cannot extend to those instruments.
